1
00:00:07,225 --> 00:00:10,025
Last time, we found three animal groups.

2
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:12,325
Amphibians, birds and fish.

3
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:13,885
Three more to go!

4
00:00:14,018 --> 00:00:15,498
An ant and a spider.

5
00:00:15,648 --> 00:00:17,368
Which one is the insect?

6
00:00:19,874 --> 00:00:21,474
It's You against the Buddies.

7
00:00:21,734 --> 00:00:23,054
You lock in first.

8
00:00:23,324 --> 00:00:25,144
One finger for every point.

9
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:27,914
A little animal is hiding in this video.

10
00:00:28,164 --> 00:00:29,404
Can you spot it?

11
00:00:30,713 --> 00:00:31,593
Round one.

12
00:00:31,913 --> 00:00:33,533
Which one is an insect?

13
00:00:33,823 --> 00:00:34,923
One, the ant.

14
00:00:35,193 --> 00:00:36,283
Two, the spider.

15
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:38,073
Show me with your fingers.

16
00:00:43,547 --> 00:00:44,527
Locked in!

17
00:00:44,655 --> 00:00:45,445
Two.

18
00:00:45,735 --> 00:00:47,605
It is tiny, and it crawls.

19
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:48,955
Like a bug!

20
00:00:49,005 --> 00:00:49,635
One!

21
00:00:49,765 --> 00:00:50,645
The ant!

22
00:00:50,697 --> 00:00:51,417
One!

23
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:52,817
But how do we know?

24
00:00:53,807 --> 00:00:55,047
Today you'll learn...

25
00:00:55,212 --> 00:00:56,662
How to spot an insect.

26
00:00:56,823 --> 00:00:58,323
How to spot a reptile.

27
00:00:58,484 --> 00:01:00,054
What cold-blooded means.

28
00:01:00,706 --> 00:01:01,645
Are you ready?

29
00:01:02,086 --> 00:01:02,855
Three!

30
00:01:03,236 --> 00:01:03,895
Two!

31
00:01:04,266 --> 00:01:04,915
One!

32
00:01:05,335 --> 00:01:06,055
Go!

33
00:01:07,344 --> 00:01:08,444
Count with me!

34
00:01:08,855 --> 00:01:11,034
One, two, three, four, five, six.

35
00:01:11,444 --> 00:01:12,504
Six legs!

36
00:01:12,642 --> 00:01:14,212
Two feelers on its head.

37
00:01:14,483 --> 00:01:16,073
And three body parts.

38
00:01:16,585 --> 00:01:17,706
Now the spider.

39
00:01:18,055 --> 00:01:19,005
Eight legs!

40
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:20,415
No feelers.

41
00:01:20,685 --> 00:01:21,925
Two body parts.

42
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:23,919
The ant is the insect!

43
00:01:24,179 --> 00:01:25,609
The spider is not.

44
00:01:25,879 --> 00:01:27,620
It belongs to a different group.

45
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:29,419
One finger?

46
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:30,930
One finger up!

47
00:01:30,981 --> 00:01:31,631
Oops!

48
00:01:32,031 --> 00:01:33,291
Count the legs!

49
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:35,170
Say it with me!

50
00:01:35,881 --> 00:01:38,511
Insects have six legs and a pair of feelers.

51
00:01:38,521 --> 00:01:42,911
The body of insects is divided into the head, thorax and abdomen.

52
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:54,600
Insects have an outer covering that is usually hard and shell-like.

53
00:01:55,114 --> 00:01:57,944
Many adult insects have two pairs of wings.

54
00:01:58,224 --> 00:02:01,264
Some adult insects have only one pair of wings.

55
00:02:01,534 --> 00:02:03,294
Some do not have wings at all.

56
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:05,680
My rule!

57
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:07,810
If it has wings, it is an insect.

58
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:08,810
A butterfly.

59
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,880
A pigeon.

60
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:11,200
Both insects!

61
00:02:11,472 --> 00:02:13,032
Something is not right.

62
00:02:13,302 --> 00:02:15,482
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

63
00:02:15,762 --> 00:02:16,722
Hold on!

64
00:02:22,235 --> 00:02:23,365
Arms crossed?

65
00:02:23,625 --> 00:02:24,795
One finger up!

66
00:02:25,085 --> 00:02:26,605
A pigeon has feathers.

67
00:02:26,875 --> 00:02:27,965
It is a bird.

68
00:02:28,245 --> 00:02:30,065
Count the legs, not the wings!

69
00:02:30,423 --> 00:02:31,153
Oops.

70
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:32,773
Six legs, not wings!

71
00:02:34,056 --> 00:02:35,056
Round two.

72
00:02:35,356 --> 00:02:36,576
A monitor lizard!

73
00:02:36,886 --> 00:02:38,776
Its skin is dry and scaly.

74
00:02:39,056 --> 00:02:39,946
Which group?

75
00:02:40,286 --> 00:02:41,636
One, amphibians.

76
00:02:41,906 --> 00:02:43,246
Two, reptiles.

77
00:02:43,526 --> 00:02:44,646
Three, mammals.

78
00:02:44,926 --> 00:02:46,406
Show me with your fingers.

79
00:02:51,878 --> 00:02:52,858
Locked in!

80
00:02:52,986 --> 00:02:53,726
One!

81
00:02:53,836 --> 00:02:55,586
Four legs, like a frog.

82
00:02:55,639 --> 00:02:56,569
Two.

83
00:02:56,679 --> 00:02:58,799
Its skin is dry, not moist.

84
00:02:58,851 --> 00:02:59,471
Two!

85
00:02:59,641 --> 00:03:00,931
Lizards like me!

86
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:02,520
The answer is two.

87
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,980
Reptiles!

88
00:03:06,848 --> 00:03:07,878
Two fingers?

89
00:03:08,148 --> 00:03:09,368
One finger up!

90
00:03:09,416 --> 00:03:10,336
I knew it!

91
00:03:10,406 --> 00:03:11,596
I'm a reptile!

92
00:03:12,024 --> 00:03:15,004
Most reptiles, except snakes, have four legs.

93
00:03:15,285 --> 00:03:18,075
Reptiles usually have dry and scaly skin.

94
00:03:18,355 --> 00:03:20,025
They breathe through their lungs.

95
00:03:20,315 --> 00:03:23,055
Most reptiles reproduce by laying eggs.

96
00:03:23,113 --> 00:03:24,433
I hatched from an egg!

97
00:03:24,782 --> 00:03:25,792
Be a scale!

98
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:27,062
Shrink down.

99
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:28,272
Quietly.

100
00:03:30,557 --> 00:03:33,277
You are one scale on a monitor lizard's back.

101
00:03:33,717 --> 00:03:35,387
You are dry, and tough.

102
00:03:35,893 --> 00:03:36,993
Early morning.

103
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:39,563
The air is cool, so you are cool.

104
00:03:39,993 --> 00:03:41,463
The lizard is slow.

105
00:03:41,906 --> 00:03:43,576
Now it crawls into the sun.

106
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:45,516
Sunlight lands on you.

107
00:03:45,936 --> 00:03:47,006
You warm up!

108
00:03:47,817 --> 00:03:49,517
At noon, it is too hot.

109
00:03:49,997 --> 00:03:50,857
Splash!

110
00:03:51,317 --> 00:03:52,657
Into the cool lake.

111
00:03:53,117 --> 00:03:54,297
You cool down.

112
00:03:58,895 --> 00:04:00,045
Say it with me!

113
00:04:00,761 --> 00:04:02,791
Reptiles are cold-blooded animals.

114
00:04:02,831 --> 00:04:06,451
This means that they do not have a constant body temperature like

115
00:04:06,201 --> 00:04:07,061
humans.

116
00:04:07,311 --> 00:04:11,261
Their body temperature changes with the environment that they are in.

117
00:04:16,212 --> 00:04:18,912
Cold-blooded does not mean I am always cold.

118
00:04:19,122 --> 00:04:20,502
I warm up in the sun!

119
00:04:21,005 --> 00:04:22,465
Show me your score hand!

120
00:04:22,755 --> 00:04:23,785
More than two?

121
00:04:24,065 --> 00:04:25,435
You beat the Buddies.

122
00:04:25,735 --> 00:04:26,795
Three fingers?

123
00:04:27,075 --> 00:04:28,085
High five!

124
00:04:28,732 --> 00:04:30,472
Did you spot the hidden animal?

125
00:04:30,762 --> 00:04:33,152
It was the grasshopper, on the lamp post!

126
00:04:33,402 --> 00:04:34,712
Is it an insect?

127
00:04:34,982 --> 00:04:36,282
Tell someone at home.

128
00:04:37,011 --> 00:04:39,211
Let's read today's key words together!

129
00:04:39,501 --> 00:04:40,261
Ready?

130
00:04:40,598 --> 00:04:41,377
Insects.

131
00:04:42,851 --> 00:04:44,511
Head, thorax, abdomen.

132
00:04:46,547 --> 00:04:47,455
Reptiles.

133
00:04:49,103 --> 00:04:50,183
Cold-blooded.

134
00:04:51,723 --> 00:04:52,663
Well done!

135
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,890
Next: this animal has wings.

136
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:57,450
It flies at night.

137
00:04:57,730 --> 00:04:58,790
Is it a bird?

138
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,670
Find out in Part Two!

139
00:05:02,335 --> 00:05:03,439
Say it with us!

140
00:05:04,239 --> 00:05:04,989
Ready?

141
00:05:05,112 --> 00:05:05,772
One!

142
00:05:06,112 --> 00:05:06,812
two!

143
00:05:07,117 --> 00:05:08,292
Now you know!
